# BizzyBoat FCU parameter customizations (diffs from baseline)
#
# These parameters override the factory baseline. Apply with:
#   mavproxy: param load bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param
#   or set individually via mavros param service
#
# ArduPilot body frame: X = forward, Y = right, Z = down

# GPS antenna offsets (applied 2026-04-02)
# GPS1 (CAN 124) = forward antenna, GPS2 = aft antenna
GPS_POS1_X       0.835000
GPS_POS1_Y       0.000000
GPS_POS1_Z       -0.890000
GPS_POS2_X       -0.835000
GPS_POS2_Y       0.000000
GPS_POS2_Z       -0.890000

# Moving baseline RTK (dual-antenna heading)
GPS_MB1_TYPE     1
GPS_MB1_OFS_X    1.670000
GPS_MB1_OFS_Y    0.000000
GPS_MB1_OFS_Z    0.000000

# IMU position offsets (applied 2026-04-07)
# Cube Orange in AutoNav box, ~0.99m aft and ~0.05m above base_link
# Measured from IzzyBoat AutoNav photos (same model)
INS_POS1_X       -0.990000
INS_POS1_Y       0.000000
INS_POS1_Z       -0.050000
INS_POS2_X       -0.990000
INS_POS2_Y       0.000000
INS_POS2_Z       -0.050000
INS_POS3_X       -0.990000
INS_POS3_Y       0.000000
INS_POS3_Z       -0.050000

# Battery monitor — BizzyBoat = EchoBoat 240 with 2× Torqeedo Power 24-3500
# in parallel. Factory baseline values describe hardware that does not
# exist on this boat (analog current sensor) and a capacity far below
# the actual pack. See issue #55.
#
# There is no current sensor wired to the Cube on BizzyBoat, so the
# analog current reading drifts around zero and BatteryState.percentage
# gets stuck at 0.99. Switch to voltage-only monitoring.
#
# Torqeedo Power 24-3500 spec (EchoBoat_240_Manual_V.pdf, Table 6, p. 25):
#   Rated voltage:       25.64 V
#   Final charge:        29.05 V  (full)
#   Final discharge:     21.00 V  (mfr minimum — damage below)
#   Usable energy:       3500 Wh per pack × 2 = 7000 Wh
#   At 25.64 V nominal:  7000 / 25.64 ≈ 273 Ah = 273 000 mAh
# Storage guidance (p. 76): 22.6–24.2 VDC, never below 22.6 V.
#
# Voltage thresholds account for the ~1.7 V terminal sag at the
# field-measured 67 A peak draw (R_internal ≈ 25 mΩ — see
# 2026-04-27 deployment debrief). LOW gives a head-home buffer
# above the storage floor; CRT keeps margin above the 21.0 V damage
# point even with sustained heavy load.
#
# FCU-side failsafes stay off (BATT_FS_LOW_ACT=0, BATT_FS_CRT_ACT=0) —
# autonomy decisions are owned by the ROS stack, not the FCU.
BATT_MONITOR     3             # voltage only (was 4: voltage + current)
BATT_CAPACITY    273000        # 2× Torqeedo 24-3500 (was 16000 from IzzyBoat)
BATT_CURR_PIN    -1            # disable unconnected ADC (was 15)
BATT_LOW_VOLT    23.0          # head-home buffer above mfr storage floor 22.6 V
BATT_CRT_VOLT    21.5          # just above mfr operating minimum 21.0 V

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Differential (skid-steer) drivetrain — applied to the FCU 2026-08-04
#
# *** TEMPORARY — REVERT WHEN THE STEERING SERVOS ARE REPLACED ***
#
# This whole block is a stopgap for running without steering servos. When
# the servos are refitted, restore the vectored-thrust drivetrain by
# setting these six params back:
#
#   SERVO1_FUNCTION  70     (Throttle)
#   SERVO2_FUNCTION  70     (Throttle)
#   SERVO3_FUNCTION  26     (GroundSteering)
#   SERVO4_FUNCTION  26     (GroundSteering)
#   TURN_RADIUS      0.5
#   PILOT_STEER_TYPE 0
#
# and delete this block. SERVO3/4_REVERSED are already 1 in the baseline
# and were left untouched, so they need no action. The authoritative
# pre-change state is 2026-08-04_pre_differential_drive.parm (938 params,
# captured immediately before the conversion) — diff against it to confirm
# a clean restore. The matching Nav2/helm reversion is described in
# config/nav2_overlay.yaml and config/bizzyboat.yaml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# BizzyBoat's two steering servos FAILED during the 2026-08-03 Broadkill
# River deployment (operator reported difficulty steering plus a strange
# noise on the return leg). They were REMOVED and both outdrives fixed
# pointing aft, so the boat is a differential (skid-steer) vehicle from
# 2026-08-04. It is no longer the directed-/vectored-thrust boat that
# older docs describe.
#
# WITHOUT THIS BLOCK a `param load` of this file, or an FCU replacement
# restored from it, would put throttle-plus-ground-steering config back
# on a boat that has no steering servos — the outdrives would receive a
# common throttle and nothing would steer.
#
# Pre-change full dump: 2026-08-04_pre_differential_drive.parm (938
# params). Skid-steer reference for a DIFFERENT hull:
# docs/izzyboat_fcu_params_live.txt — drivetrain block only; Izzy
# diverges on ~90 other meaningful params.
#
# Output mapping established 2026-08-04 by disabling SERVO2 and seeing
# which prop still ran, then confirmed by an out-of-water RC direction
# check (forward / astern / turning all correct) and 5 h of GUIDED
# survey: OUTPUT 1 = PORT, OUTPUT 2 = STARBOARD.
SERVO1_FUNCTION  73            # ThrottleLeft  = PORT   (was 70 Throttle)
SERVO2_FUNCTION  74            # ThrottleRight = STBD   (was 70 Throttle)
SERVO3_FUNCTION  0             # steering servo removed (was 26 GroundSteering)
SERVO4_FUNCTION  0             # steering servo removed (was 26 GroundSteering)
TURN_RADIUS      0.0           # skid steer turns in place (was 0.5)
PILOT_STEER_TYPE 3             # was 0; matches IzzyBoat. Keeps RC steering
                               # direction unchanged when backing up instead
                               # of inverting car-style. RC/MANUAL path only —
                               # does not affect the GUIDED autonomy path.
#
# NOT CHANGED, deliberately — this file records what is actually on the
# FCU, and everything below ran a full 5 h GUIDED survey on 2026-08-04
# without trouble. Do not "improve" them from a desk:
#   SERVO1/2_MIN 1000 / MAX 2000 / TRIM 1500 — leave. Do NOT copy Izzy's
#     SERVO1_MIN 1350; that encodes Izzy's limited-reverse ESCs, and full
#     reverse range is needed for pivots and the Nav2 reverse behaviour.
#   ATC_STR_RAT_* / ATC_STR_ACC_MAX — the stock steering-rate loop tracked
#     fine in GUIDED all day. Measured peak yaw is 0.62 rad/s (35 deg/s),
#     well under the 120 deg/s ATC_STR_RAT_MAX ceiling, so the ceiling is
#     not binding and there is no windup to fix.
#   MOT_THST_ASYM 1.0 — validated: mean forward creep while pivoting is
#     +0.058 m/s over 21527 samples, i.e. forward and reverse thrust are
#     near enough symmetric.
#   MOT_STR_THR_MIX 0.5 — untested lever, see below.
#   SERVO3/4_REVERSED 1 — stale flag from the vectored config; harmless
#     with both outputs disabled.
#   WP_PIVOT_ANGLE 45 / WP_PIVOT_RATE 30 — AUTO-mode waypoint params,
#     inert under Project11 (GUIDED velocity setpoints).
#
# OPEN ITEM — MOT_STR_THR_MIX. Bag analysis over 218133 samples shows the
# maximum differential the mixer delivers is exactly diff_max = 1000 -
# 2*throttle (us), i.e. ArduPilot CLIPS steering at high throttle rather
# than backing throttle off to preserve it. MOT_STR_THR_MIX (skid-steer
# only, currently 0.5) is the steering-vs-throttle prioritisation that
# governs this; raising it toward 0.9-1.0 should recover some turn
# authority at survey speed, at the cost of slowing into turns. NOT yet
# tested on the water — try it live and revert with a single param set.
# Expect partial recovery only: the hull's yaw response per unit
# differential also roughly halves between 1 m/s and survey speed
# (0.221 -> 0.109 rad/s per full differential), so the mixer is about
# half the problem, not all of it.
